---
import AppLayout from "@/layouts/AppLayout.astro";
import { getAllApps } from "@/lib/apps";
const entry = (await getAllApps()).find(({ data }) => data.slug === "movecut");
if (!entry) throw new Error("MoveCut app entry is missing.");
const app = entry.data;
---

<AppLayout
  app={app}
  locale="en"
  title="MoveCut Privacy Policy"
  description="How MoveCut handles photos, workout details, device permissions, storage, sharing, and support requests."
  canonical="/movecut/privacy/en/"
>
  <div class="shell legal-shell">
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/movecut/">MoveCut</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span
        >Privacy Policy</span
      >
    </nav>
    <header class="legal-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">MoveCut legal</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p>
        How MoveCut handles your photos, workout details, and device
        permissions.
      </p>
      <div class="legal-meta">
        <span>Version 2026-09-09</span><span>Effective September 9, 2026</span>
      </div>
    </header>
    <div class="legal-grid">
      <aside class="legal-sidebar">
        <nav aria-label="On this page">
          <h2>On this page</h2>
          <ol>
            <li><a href="#scope">Scope and operator</a></li>
            <li><a href="#local-data">Data handled on your device</a></li>
            <li><a href="#permissions">Permissions and choices</a></li>
            <li><a href="#storage">Storage, saving, and sharing</a></li>
            <li><a href="#services">Stores, backups, and this website</a></li>
            <li><a href="#deletion">Retention and deletion</a></li>
            <li><a href="#contact">Your rights and contact</a></li>
            <li><a href="#children">Children and security</a></li>
            <li><a href="#changes">Changes</a></li>
          </ol>
        </nav>
        <a href="/movecut/support/">MoveCut Support →</a>
      </aside>
      <article class="legal-content">
        <h2 id="scope">1. Scope and operator</h2>
        <p>
          This policy explains how ROKGG (the “operator”) handles information in
          the MoveCut mobile app. MoveCut turns workout photos and details into
          image cards.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Operator and privacy contact:</strong> ROKGG · <a
            href="mailto:notice.rokgg@gmail.com">notice.rokgg@gmail.com</a
          >
        </p>

        <h2 id="local-data">2. Data handled on your device</h2>
        <p>
          MoveCut has no registration, login, account sync, advertising,
          analytics SDK, or operator-run server upload. The app processes the
          following information locally when you choose or enter it:
        </p>
        <table>
          <thead
            ><tr><th>Information</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Location</th></tr
            ></thead
          >
          <tbody>
            <tr
              ><td>Photos you select or take</td><td>Create and edit cards</td
              ><td>MoveCut’s on-device app storage</td></tr
            >
            <tr
              ><td>Activity, date, time, distance, and note</td><td
                >Display your card and library entry</td
              ><td>MoveCut’s on-device app storage</td></tr
            >
            <tr
              ><td>Template, aspect ratio, colors, crop, and zoom</td><td
                >Restore your edit</td
              ><td>MoveCut’s on-device app storage</td></tr
            >
            <tr
              ><td>App preferences and local record identifiers</td><td
                >Remember settings and distinguish records</td
              ><td>MoveCut’s on-device app storage</td></tr
            >
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p>
          MoveCut may resize a selected photo into an app-managed copy for
          editing. It does not upload your photos, workout details, finished
          cards, or photo EXIF metadata to the operator.
        </p>

        <h2 id="permissions">3. Permissions and choices</h2>
        <p>
          Camera access is requested only when you choose to take a photo. Photo
          selection uses the operating system’s photo picker. Saving a finished
          card may request permission to add it to your photo library, depending
          on your device and operating system.
        </p>
        <p>
          MoveCut does not use the microphone, contacts, precise location, or
          advertising tracking. If you decline a permission, you can continue
          using features that do not need it. You can change permissions at any
          time in your device settings.
        </p>

        <h2 id="storage">4. Storage, saving, and sharing</h2>
        <p>
          Saving a card inside MoveCut stores an app-managed photo copy, card
          image, and edit details on your device. Deleting an entry from My
          Cards also asks the app to delete its related app-managed files.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you save a finished PNG to Photos, that file is separate from
          MoveCut’s library. Delete it in the Photos app if you no longer want
          it. If you choose Share, MoveCut passes only the finished image to the
          operating system share sheet and the app you select. The recipient
          app’s privacy policy applies after sharing.
        </p>

        <h2 id="services">5. App stores, device backups, and this website</h2>
        <p>
          MoveCut does not send app content to advertising or analytics
          services. Apple or Google may separately process purchase,
          installation, update, security, and purchase-restoration information
          under their own privacy policies.
        </p>
        <p>
          Your operating system and Apple iCloud or Google account settings may
          include MoveCut data in a device backup. The operator cannot access
          those backups. Backup availability, retention, and deletion are
          controlled by your device and backup provider.
        </p>
        <p>
          This policy and the support page are hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub
          may process technical logs, such as an IP address, to deliver and
          secure the website. See the <a
            href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement"
            >GitHub General Privacy Statement</a
          > and <a
            href="https://docs.github.com/en/pages/getting-started-with-github-pages/what-is-github-pages#data-collection"
            >GitHub Pages data collection notice</a
          >. These pages do not include visitor analytics scripts.
        </p>

        <h2 id="deletion">6. Retention and deletion</h2>
        <p>
          MoveCut keeps local photos, cards, workout details, and preferences
          until you delete a record, clear app data, or delete the app. Copies
          saved to Photos, included in a device backup, or sent to another app
          must be deleted through that photo library, backup service, or
          recipient app.
        </p>
        <p>
          The operator cannot look up or delete information stored only inside
          the app because it is never received by the operator. You may revoke
          camera or photo access in device settings at any time.
        </p>

        <h2 id="contact">7. Your rights and contact</h2>
        <p>
          If you email support, the operator receives your email address and
          message to answer your request. You may ask to access, correct, or
          delete that correspondence when no legal retention duty applies.
          Contact <a href="mailto:notice.rokgg@gmail.com"
            >notice.rokgg@gmail.com</a
          > and include “MoveCut” in the subject.
        </p>

        <h2 id="children">8. Age restriction and security</h2>
        <p>
          MoveCut is intended for users aged 18 and older and does not permit
          use by anyone under 18. MoveCut does not ask for an age or create user
          accounts, so it cannot verify every user’s age.
        </p>
        <p>
          MoveCut relies on the operating system’s app sandbox and permission
          controls. Use a device passcode and current operating system security
          updates to help protect locally stored information.
        </p>

        <h2 id="changes">9. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          If MoveCut’s data handling or external services change, this page will
          be updated with a new version and effective date. This policy is
          effective September 9, 2026.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</AppLayout>
